---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
const states = ['Alabama','Alaska','Arizona','Arkansas','California','Colorado','Connecticut','Delaware','District of Columbia','Florida','Georgia','Hawaii','Idaho','Illinois','Indiana','Iowa','Kansas','Kentucky','Louisiana','Maine','Maryland','Massachusetts','Michigan','Minnesota','Mississippi','Missouri','Montana','Nebraska','Nevada','New Hampshire','New Jersey','New Mexico','New York','North Carolina','North Dakota','Ohio','Oklahoma','Oregon','Pennsylvania','Puerto Rico','Rhode Island','South Carolina','South Dakota','Tennessee','Texas','Utah','Vermont','Virginia','Washington','West Virginia','Wisconsin','Wyoming','Guam','U.S. Virgin Islands','American Samoa','Northern Mariana Islands'];
---
<Base title="Petition" description="Sign the petition to the White House, the courts and Congress: fair treatment for Eva Xie, respectful reform of how ICE interacts with the public, and mutual respect between the United States and China.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="zh-title" lang="zh-Hant">連署請願</p>
      <h1>Sign the petition.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Fair treatment for Eva. Respectful enforcement for everyone. Mutual respect between all people and
        countries, especially the United States and China.
      </p>
      <p class="count-line" aria-live="polite">
        <span class="count-num" id="sig-count">&nbsp;</span>
        <span id="sig-count-label" class="muted"></span>
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="#sign">Add your name</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="#statement">Read the petition</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="statement">
    <div class="narrow petition-text">
      <p class="eyebrow">The petition</p>
      <h2>Fair treatment, respectful enforcement, mutual respect</h2>
      <p class="muted small">
        To the President and the White House; the executive branch, including the Department of Homeland
        Security, U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement and the Department of Justice; the judicial branch,
        including the federal courts and the immigration courts; and our elected representatives in Congress:
      </p>

      <p>
        We are students, scholars, neighbors and fellow Americans. We support the lawful mission of
        immigration enforcement. A nation has the right to decide who enters and who stays, and the officers
        who carry out that work deserve our respect. We also believe that how that power is used matters, and
        that enforcement is strongest when it earns the public's trust.
      </p>
      <p>
        On November 19, 2026, Eva Xie, a PhD student in neuroscience at Princeton University, was detained by
        ICE at Ronald Reagan Washington National Airport as she returned from Neuroscience 2026, the annual
        meeting of the Society for Neuroscience. Eva came to the United States with her family at age 14 and
        has lived here since. She is a student and a researcher, not a threat.
      </p>

      <h3>We respectfully ask:</h3>
      <ol class="asks">
        <li>
          <strong>Fair treatment for Eva Xie.</strong>
          That she be treated with dignity and humane care while in custody; that she have prompt and
          regular access to her attorney, her family and her university; that her case be reviewed quickly
          and fairly; and that she be released to continue her studies while it is decided.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reform of how ICE interacts with the public.</strong>
          That officers identify themselves and clearly explain why a person is being stopped or held, in a
          language they understand; that detention be a last resort for people with deep community ties who
          pose no danger; that families, attorneys, consulates and universities be notified promptly; and
          that every person be treated with dignity, whatever their status.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Mutual respect between all people and countries, especially the United States and China.</strong>
          That students and scholars be welcomed as bridges between nations, not treated as suspects
          because of where they were born; and that our government show visitors the same respect we expect
          for Americans who study, work and travel abroad.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Of each branch of government, we ask:</h3>
      <ul class="branches">
        <li>
          <strong>The White House and the executive branch.</strong>
          Set clear, published standards for how ICE and CBP treat students, scholars and visitors in valid
          status, and see that they are followed: use discretion, explain every stop and detention, ensure
          prompt access to counsel and consulates, and keep detention a last resort. Review Eva's case
          promptly and use the discretion the law already provides to release her while it is decided.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The judicial branch.</strong>
          We respect the independence of the courts and ask only for what the law promises everyone: that
          Eva's case, and every case like hers, be heard promptly and fairly, with full due process and
          meaningful access to counsel.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Congress.</strong>
          Exercise oversight of how immigration enforcement treats students and scholars, and support clear
          guidance on access to counsel, timely notice to families and universities, and alternatives to
          detention.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <blockquote>
        Supporting enforcement and asking it to do better are not opposites. Mutual respect is the basis for
        collaboration.
        <span class="zh" lang="zh-Hant">相互尊重是合作的基礎。</span>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="sign" class="sign-section">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Add your name</p>
      <h2>Sign the petition</h2>

      <div id="sign-closed" class="card notice" hidden>
        <h3>Online signing opens soon</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          We are finishing the setup. In the meantime, you can add your name by emailing
          <a href={`mailto:${site.links.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Sign the petition')}`}>{site.links.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <form id="sign-form" class="card sign-form" novalidate>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="f-name">Full name <span class="req">required</span></label>
          <input id="f-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" maxlength="80" required />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="f-email">Email <span class="opt">optional</span></label>
          <input id="f-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" maxlength="254" />
          <p class="hint">Add it to get a confirmation email and a link to remove your signature later. Your email is never shown publicly or shared.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="f-phone">Phone <span class="opt">optional</span></label>
          <input id="f-phone" name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" maxlength="30" />
          <p class="hint">Only the campaign team sees it, to reach you about the campaign if needed. Never shown publicly or shared.</p>
        </div>

        <p class="opt-head">Everything below is optional, but it helps us show lawmakers and the university who is behind this.</p>
        <div class="field-row">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-city">City or town</label>
            <input id="f-city" name="city" type="text" autocomplete="address-level2" maxlength="80" placeholder="e.g. Princeton" />
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-state">State</label>
            <select id="f-state" name="state" autocomplete="address-level1">
              <option value="">Choose…</option>
              {states.map((st) => <option value={st}>{st}</option>)}
              <option value="Outside the U.S.">Outside the U.S.</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div class="field zip">
            <label for="f-zip">ZIP code</label>
            <input id="f-zip" name="zip" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="postal-code" maxlength="10" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="hint">State and ZIP let us tell each member of Congress how many of their constituents signed. Your ZIP code is never shown publicly.</p>

        <div class="field-row two">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-aff">Princeton connection</label>
            <select id="f-aff" name="affiliation">
              <option value="">Choose…</option>
              <option value="student">Princeton student</option>
              <option value="faculty_staff">Princeton faculty or staff</option>
              <option value="alum">Princeton alum</option>
              <option value="community">Community member</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="f-heard">How did you hear about this?</label>
            <select id="f-heard" name="heardFrom">
              <option value="">Choose…</option>
              <option value="qr">QR code (shirt, poster, sticker)</option>
              <option value="social">Social media</option>
              <option value="rally">Rally or event</option>
              <option value="friend">Friend or colleague</option>
              <option value="news">News story</option>
              <option value="email">Email or group chat</option>
              <option value="other">Other</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label for="f-comment">Why I'm signing</label>
          <textarea id="f-comment" name="comment" rows="3" maxlength="500"></textarea>
          <p class="hint">Up to 500 characters. Not posted automatically. If you sign publicly, we may quote it with your name.</p>
        </div>

        <fieldset class="field privacy">
          <legend>Show my signature</legend>
          <label class="choice">
            <input type="radio" name="public" value="true" checked />
            <span><strong>Publicly.</strong> Show my name (and city and state, if given) on the list of signers below.</span>
          </label>
          <label class="choice">
            <input type="radio" name="public" value="false" />
            <span><strong>Privately.</strong> Count my signature, but do not show my name anywhere.</span>
          </label>
        </fieldset>

        <label class="choice check">
          <input type="checkbox" name="agree" required />
          <span>I have read and agree with the petition above.</span>
        </label>
        <label class="choice check">
          <input type="checkbox" name="updates" />
          <span>You may contact me with campaign updates by email or phone. <span class="muted">(optional)</span></span>
        </label>

        <!-- Spam trap: hidden from people, filled in by bots. -->
        <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
          <label>Website <input type="text" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" /></label>
        </div>

        <div id="turnstile-box"></div>

        <p id="form-error" class="form-error" role="alert" hidden></p>
        <button class="btn" type="submit" id="sign-btn">Sign the petition</button>
        <p class="hint">
          We record your name, the time you signed and anything else you fill in. If you give an email, you can
          remove your signature at any time with the link in your confirmation email, or write to us.
        </p>
      </form>

      <div id="sign-done" class="card done" hidden tabindex="-1">
        <p class="eyebrow">Thank you</p>
        <h3 id="done-title">You signed the petition.</h3>
        <p id="done-time" class="muted"></p>
        <p id="done-email" class="muted"></p>
        <p>The next step is the most powerful one: share it with one more person.</p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <button class="btn" type="button" id="share-btn">Share the petition</button>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/free-eva/#act">More ways to help</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="signers">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Signers</p>
      <h2>Who has signed</h2>
      <p class="muted small" id="signers-note">Signers who chose to be listed publicly, newest first. Signers who chose privacy are counted in the total but not shown.</p>
      <ul id="signer-list" class="signer-list"></ul>
      <p id="signers-empty" class="muted" hidden>Be the first to sign publicly.</p>
      <button class="btn ghost" type="button" id="more-btn" hidden>Show more</button>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<script>
  type Signer = { name: string; city: string | null; state?: string | null; signedAt: string };
  type PetitionData = { ready: boolean; count: number; signers: Signer[]; nextCursor: number | null; turnstileSiteKey: string | null };

  const $ = <T extends HTMLElement>(id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as T;
  const form = $<HTMLFormElement>('sign-form');
  const errorEl = $('form-error');
  const btn = $<HTMLButtonElement>('sign-btn');
  const list = $<HTMLUListElement>('signer-list');
  const moreBtn = $<HTMLButtonElement>('more-btn');
  let cursor: number | null = null;
  let turnstileWidget: string | undefined;

  const fmtTime = (iso: string) =>
    new Date(iso).toLocaleString(undefined, { dateStyle: 'medium', timeStyle: 'short' });

  function setCount(n: number) {
    $('sig-count').textContent = n.toLocaleString();
    $('sig-count-label').textContent = n === 1 ? 'person has signed' : 'people have signed';
  }

  function addSigners(signers: Signer[], prepend = false) {
    for (const s of signers) {
      const li = document.createElement('li');
      const name = document.createElement('span');
      name.className = 'sn';
      name.textContent = s.name; // textContent: never render signer input as HTML
      li.append(name);
      const place = [s.city, s.state].filter(Boolean).join(', ');
      if (place) {
        const city = document.createElement('span');
        city.className = 'sc';
        city.textContent = place;
        li.append(city);
      }
      const t = document.createElement('time');
      t.dateTime = s.signedAt;
      t.textContent = fmtTime(s.signedAt);
      li.append(t);
      prepend ? list.prepend(li) : list.append(li);
    }
    $('signers-empty').hidden = list.children.length > 0;
  }

  async function load(more = false) {
    try {
      const res = await fetch(`/api/petition${more && cursor ? `?cursor=${cursor}` : ''}`);
      if (!res.ok) throw new Error(String(res.status));
      const data = (await res.json()) as PetitionData;
      if (!more) {
        if (!data.ready) {
          form.hidden = true;
          $('sign-closed').hidden = false;
          $('signers').hidden = true;
          return;
        }
        setCount(data.count);
        if (data.turnstileSiteKey) mountTurnstile(data.turnstileSiteKey);
      }
      addSigners(data.signers);
      cursor = data.nextCursor;
      moreBtn.hidden = !cursor;
    } catch {
      // API not reachable (for example `astro dev` without the Worker). Keep the form visible.
      $('signers-empty').hidden = false;
    }
  }

  function mountTurnstile(siteKey: string) {
    const s = document.createElement('script');
    s.src = 'https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js?render=explicit';
    s.async = true;
    s.onload = () => {
      // @ts-ignore turnstile is a global from the script above
      turnstileWidget = window.turnstile.render('#turnstile-box', { sitekey: siteKey, theme: 'dark' });
    };
    document.head.append(s);
  }

  function showError(msg: string, field?: string) {
    errorEl.textContent = msg;
    errorEl.hidden = false;
    if (field) (form.elements.namedItem(field) as HTMLElement | null)?.focus();
  }

  form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    errorEl.hidden = true;
    const fd = new FormData(form);
    const name = String(fd.get('name') || '').trim();
    const email = String(fd.get('email') || '').trim();
    if (name.length < 2) return showError('Please enter your name.', 'name');
    if (email && !/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]{2,}$/.test(email)) return showError('Please enter a valid email address.', 'email');
    if (!fd.get('agree')) return showError('Please tick the box to confirm you agree with the petition.', 'agree');

    const payload = {
      name,
      email,
      city: String(fd.get('city') || '').trim(),
      state: String(fd.get('state') || ''),
      zip: String(fd.get('zip') || '').trim(),
      phone: String(fd.get('phone') || '').trim(),
      affiliation: String(fd.get('affiliation') || ''),
      heardFrom: String(fd.get('heardFrom') || ''),
      comment: String(fd.get('comment') || '').trim(),
      public: fd.get('public') === 'true',
      agree: true,
      updates: Boolean(fd.get('updates')),
      website: String(fd.get('website') || ''),
      turnstileToken: String(fd.get('cf-turnstile-response') || ''),
    };

    btn.disabled = true;
    btn.textContent = 'Signing…';
    try {
      const res = await fetch('/api/petition/sign', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(payload),
      });
      const data = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));
      if (!res.ok || !data.ok) {
        showError(data.error || 'Something went wrong. Please try again.', data.field);
        // @ts-ignore
        if (turnstileWidget !== undefined) window.turnstile?.reset(turnstileWidget);
        return;
      }
      form.hidden = true;
      const done = $('sign-done');
      done.hidden = false;
      $('done-title').textContent = `Thank you, ${name.split(' ')[0]}. You signed the petition.`;
      $('done-time').textContent = `Signed ${fmtTime(data.signedAt)}. ${payload.public ? 'Your name is on the public list below.' : 'Your signature is private: it is counted but not shown.'}`;
      $('done-email').textContent = data.emailQueued ? `A confirmation email is on its way to ${email}.` : '';
      if (typeof data.count === 'number') setCount(data.count);
      if (payload.public) addSigners([{ name, city: payload.city || null, state: payload.state || null, signedAt: data.signedAt }], true);
      done.focus();
    } catch {
      showError('We could not reach the server. Check your connection and try again.');
    } finally {
      btn.disabled = false;
      btn.textContent = 'Sign the petition';
    }
  });

  $('share-btn').addEventListener('click', async () => {
    const url = `${location.origin}/petition/`;
    const text = 'I signed the petition for fair treatment for Eva Xie and mutual respect. Add your name:';
    if (navigator.share) {
      try { await navigator.share({ title: 'Free Eva petition', text, url }); } catch { /* cancelled */ }
    } else {
      await navigator.clipboard?.writeText(url);
      $('share-btn').textContent = 'Link copied';
    }
  });

  moreBtn.addEventListener('click', () => load(true));
  load();
</script>

<style>
  .count-line { margin: 1.4rem 0 0; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.6rem; flex-wrap: wrap; min-height: 2.6rem; }
  .count-num { font-family: var(--font-stencil); color: var(--orange); font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.8rem); line-height: 1; }

  .petition-text p, .petition-text li { font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .petition-text h3 { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .asks { padding-left: 1.3rem; display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  .asks li::marker { color: var(--orange); font-family: var(--font-stencil); }
  .branches { padding-left: 1.3rem; display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  .branches li::marker { color: var(--orange); }
  .asks strong, .branches strong { display: block; color: var(--white); margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
  blockquote .zh { display: block; margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--orange); font-size: 1rem; }

  .sign-form { display: grid; gap: 1.1rem; }
  .field { display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; margin: 0; border: 0; padding: 0; }
  .field > label, .field legend { font-weight: 600; }
  .req, .opt { font-weight: 400; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); margin-left: 0.3rem; }
  .opt-head { margin: 0.4rem 0 -0.3rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .field-row { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .field-row { grid-template-columns: 1.3fr 1.3fr 0.8fr; }
    .field-row.two { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
  .field-row + .hint { margin-top: -0.6rem; }
  textarea { resize: vertical; min-height: 5rem; }
  select { appearance: none; background-image: linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 50%, var(--muted) 50%), linear-gradient(135deg, var(--muted) 50%, transparent 50%); background-position: calc(100% - 18px) 50%, calc(100% - 13px) 50%; background-size: 5px 5px; background-repeat: no-repeat; padding-right: 2rem !important; }
  input[type='text'], input[type='email'], input[type='tel'], select, textarea {
    font: inherit; color: var(--white); background-color: var(--black); border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem; width: 100%;
  }
  input[type='text']:focus, input[type='email']:focus, input[type='tel']:focus, select:focus, textarea:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--orange); outline-offset: 1px; border-color: var(--orange); }
  .hint { font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }
  .privacy { gap: 0.55rem; }
  .privacy legend { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .choice { display: flex; gap: 0.65rem; align-items: flex-start; cursor: pointer; }
  .choice input { accent-color: var(--orange); width: 1.15rem; height: 1.15rem; margin-top: 0.25rem; flex: none; }
  .hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; }
  .form-error { color: #ffb4a8; background: color-mix(in srgb, #ff4d2e 14%, transparent); border-left: 4px solid #ff6a4d; padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem; margin: 0; }
  .sign-form .btn { justify-self: start; cursor: pointer; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .sign-form .btn:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: wait; }
  .done { border-top: 4px solid var(--orange); }
  .done .btn { cursor: pointer; font-size: 1rem; }
  .notice { border-top: 4px solid var(--orange); }

  .signer-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1.2rem 0; display: grid; gap: 0; }
  .signer-list :global(li) {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.2rem 0.8rem; align-items: baseline;
    padding: 0.65rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .signer-list :global(.sn) { font-weight: 600; }
  .signer-list :global(.sc) { color: var(--muted); }
  .signer-list :global(time) { margin-left: auto; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  #more-btn { cursor: pointer; }
</style>
